From 0d11871b23633e88b75d345f884361f1715f6dfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tarpediem <tarpediem@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:20:09 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 22/23] power: supply: max77705: optional battery temperature
 safety monitor

The driver configures the charger and enables it at probe, with no battery
temperature check, no charge current or input limit from the firmware and
the charger watchdog off. On boards where the battery thermistor sits on a
PMIC ADC (the vendor driver monitors it in software), that leaves charging
unchecked.

When the charger node has a "battery-temp" IIO channel:
- charging is disabled while the limits are written, then enabled only
  while the thermistor reads inside the monitored battery's alert-celsius
  range, with 2 C hysteresis; a failed or implausible reading disables it;
- constant-charge-current-max of the battery and the new
  input-current-limit-microamp are written at probe, and sysfs writes are
  clamped to them;
- constant-charge-voltage-max is used for the float voltage when set;
- an optional safety timer (maxim,safety-timer-sec) stops charging after
  that much charging time since the input was plugged in;
- the charger watchdog stays enabled, as in the vendor driver, and is
  kicked by the check every 10 s, so charging stops if the kernel does;
- every check rewrites the current, input and voltage limits if they are
  found above the configured ones (watchdog reset), and disables charging
  if that does not hold.

Health reports overheat, cold or safety timer expiry, and the charger
exposes the thermistor temperature. Without the channel the behaviour is
unchanged, except three fixes that apply to both:
- status was POWER_SUPPLY_CHARGE_TYPE_NONE (= "Charging") with CHG_EN off;
  it is now "Not charging" with an input and "Discharging" without;
- the input limit was written as mA / 25 while it reads back as
  (reg + 1) * 25 mA (the vendor driver writes mA / 25 - 1);
- voltage_max_design dereferenced the battery info, which is read only
  after the supply is registered; it now returns -ENODATA until then.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
